    "note": [
        {
            "structuredValue": [],
            "parallelValue": [],
            "groupedValue": [],
            "value": "\"The Earthquake Data Report (EDR) is a bulletin of all seismic phase and amplitude data which were associated with events published in the Preliminary Determination of Epicenters (PDE) Monthly Listing for the corresponding month. It also contains information about the hypocentral computations (such as standard errors) that are not included in the PDE Monthly Listing. The EDR \r\nis a technical data file intended for users who are familiar with basic seismological practice.  It is recommended that potential users who are unfamiliar with such practice should obtain first the PDE Monthly Listing (available from the U.S. Government Printing Office) before working with the \r\nEarthquake Data Report.\"",
            "type": "abstract",
            "identifier": [],
            "note": [],
            "appliesTo": []
